Subject: [PATCH] gpui: accept text dragged in from other applications on macOS

Windows on macOS register for NSFilenamesPboardType only, so a selection
dragged from another application (Notes, Safari, Mail) is refused at the
window and no element can receive it.

This registers NSPasteboardTypeString beside NSFilenamesPboardType and, when
a drag enters, reads the pasteboard file names first (so a pasteboard that
holds both, as Finder's and GPUI's own file copy do, is still a file drop
carrying ExternalPaths), else its non-empty plain text. The text is
delivered as a new FileDropEvent::TextEntered { position, text } whose drag
value is a new ExternalText, received with on_drop::<ExternalText> just as
files are received with on_drop::<ExternalPaths>; the rest of the drag is
the existing Pending, Submit, Exited and Ended events.

A platform drag's Entered, TextEntered, Pending and Submit events now count
as pointer input in the window's input modality: AppKit sends a window no
mouse-moved events during a drag, so after any keystroke the modality stayed
Keyboard, Hitbox::is_hovered answered false and a drop (of files today)
reached no on_drop handler.

The text is a type of its own, not an enum wrapping the paths, because the
drag model dispatches on_drop by the dragged value's type: wrapping the
paths would stop every existing on_drop::<ExternalPaths> handler.
FileDropEvent::Entered keeps its fields, so the Linux and Windows platforms
compile unchanged and keep their file drops; their text drops are left to
their own registration.

The paths below are those of the published gpui-pre and gpui-pre-macos
0.3.10 crates; in Zed's tree they are crates/gpui and crates/gpui_macos.

Tests: gpui_macos's window tests gain the registered types, a text-only
pasteboard read as text, file names beside text read as the files, and a
missing pasteboard, an empty one and empty text read as no drop.
